  "problem": "According to the flux form of Green's theorem, the flux of the vector field \n$F(x,y)=\u27e8y+2{x}^{2}y,\\,{x}^{2}-x{y}^{2}\u27e9$\nacross the rectangle $C$ with vertices $(0,0),(2,0),(2,1),$ and  $(0,1)$ can be represented as\n\n$$\n{\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is traversed counterclockwise, $n$ is the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C,$ and $D$ is the region bounded by $C.$ Calculate the function $f(x,y).$",
